%description:

A deviation of StochasticChannelModel from the specifications, pinned and not
endorsed: the shadow fading of an indoor UE's link has the standard deviation of
the outdoor link in its LOS state, where TR 36.873 and the single-frequency
model of TR 38.901 give an indoor UE's link 7 dB.

TR 36.873 v12.7.0 7.2.3, rows "3D-UMi O2I" and "3D-UMa O2I": "sigma_SF =7".
TR 38.901 v16.1.0 Table 7.4.3-3 ("O2I building penetration loss model for
single-frequency simulations <6 GHz"), row sigma_SF: "7 dB (note: replacing the
respective value in Table 7.4.1-1)".

The model takes the standard deviation from the path-loss strategy's
getShadowingStdDev(), which is given the deployment, the distances and the LOS
state, but not whether the UE is indoors: an indoor UMa UE gets the 4 dB (LOS)
or 6 dB (NLOS) of TR 36.873 Table 7.3-6 and TR 38.901 Table 7.4.1-1.

Checked on a UMa cell with one carrier at 2 GHz, on the first shadowing value of
the links of four indoor UEs, under the TR 38.901 and the TR 36.873 channel
model, in LOS and in NLOS. The value is one N(0, sigma) draw; it is divided by
the standard-normal draw replayed from a copy of the model's generator, which
gives sigma. ChannelModelIndoorShadowingSpec asserts the specifications as an
expected failure. When the model follows them, change this test together with
that one.

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr36873ChannelModel;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        model901: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        model873: Tr36873ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

# one carrier below 6 GHz: a single-frequency simulation
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

**.shadowing = true
**.fading = false
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *model901 = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model901");
auto *model873 = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model873");
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");

// a UMa base station and four UEs at one place, 100 m from it: a link each, so a
// first shadowing value each
StubEndpoint bsEndpoint;
bsEndpoint.nodeId = MacNodeId(1);
bsEndpoint.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
StubRadioRegistration bsRadio(medium, bsEndpoint.nodeId, &bsEndpoint);
StubEndpoint ues[4];
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubRadioRegistration>> ueRadios;
for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    ues[i].nodeId = MacNodeId(1025 + i);
    ues[i].coord = Coord(100, 0, 1.5);
    ueRadios.push_back(std::make_unique<StubRadioRegistration>(medium, ues[i].nodeId, &ues[i]));
}
const double d2D = 100.0, d3D = std::sqrt(100.0 * 100.0 + 23.5 * 23.5);

wait(0.010);

// The standard deviation a link's first shadowing value was drawn with: the
// value is one N(0, sigma) draw, replayed here as a standard-normal one from a
// copy of the model's generator, so their ratio is sigma.
auto sigmaOf = [&] (StochasticChannelModel *model, StubEndpoint& ue, bool indoor, bool los) {
    ue.insideBuilding = indoor;
    ue.insideDistance = indoor ? 10.0 : 0.0;
    ChannelModelProbe probe(model);
    RadioLink link = probe.whatIfLink(&ue, dlCqiTransmission(&bsEndpoint, ue.nodeId));
    RngSnapshot snapshot(model);
    double value = model->computeShadowing(d3D, d2D, los, link);
    return value / omnetpp::normal(snapshot.rng(), 0, 1);
};

c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: an indoor UMa UE's shadow fading under TR 38.901 has the outdoor LOS sigma, 4 dB", sigmaOf(model901, ues[0], true, true), 4.0, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: ...and the outdoor NLOS sigma, 6 dB, in NLOS", sigmaOf(model901, ues[1], true, false), 6.0, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: an indoor UMa UE's shadow fading under TR 36.873 has the outdoor LOS sigma, 4 dB", sigmaOf(model873, ues[2], true, true), 4.0, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: ...and the outdoor NLOS sigma, 6 dB, in NLOS", sigmaOf(model873, ues[3], true, false), 6.0, 1e-9);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=4 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
